  "result": "I fixed the bug. Clamping returned a value outside the range only when it clamped to an open bound (`min_open=True` or `max_open=True`). It stepped one past the bound instead of one inside it:\n\n- `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `0` or less returned `-1`; it now returns `1`.\n- `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` given `5` or more returned `6`; it now returns `4`.\n\n**The fix:** in `IntRange._clamp` (`src/click/types.py:754`), `bound - dir` is now `bound + dir`. The caller passes `dir=1` for the min bound and `-1` for the max bound, so adding `dir` moves the value into the range.\n\nThe existing tests only checked clamping to closed bounds, which is why this wasn't caught. I added the two cases above to `tests/test_types.py`. The tests in `test_types.py` and `test_info_dict.py` pass (71 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't run the rest of the test suite, and I haven't committed anything.",
